cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use, cite or build on this work, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "A5K — A Theoretical Design Proposition for an Amiga 5000-Like System"
version: "Rev. AG"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - name: 'Ryan David Hall (AKA "ProphetPX")'
abstract: >-
  A design study proposing a modern re-issue of the Amiga custom-chipset
  architecture: an Agnus-class DMA scheduler, a planar Denise-class scanout,
  a minterm blitter and an MC-1 Copper, presented on a PCIe card with a
  RISC-V host and an open-source toolchain. Includes a Copper instruction
  set, a Migen implementation skeleton, a bill of materials and a
  comparative analysis against AAA, Hombre and a 2026 scientific workstation.
keywords:
  - Amiga
  - open hardware
  - FPGA
  - RISC-V
  - Copper
  - display architecture
